{:edb/db-before-t 2135 :edb/db-after-t 2136 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535448 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:16:31.274Z" 13194139535448 true] [17592186216519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349653 13194139535448 true] [17592186216519 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349654 13194139535448 true] [17592186216519 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349653 13194139535448 true] [17592186216520 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349655 13194139535448 true] [17592186216520 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349655 13194139535448 true] [17592186216521 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349656 13194139535448 true] [17592186216521 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349656 13194139535448 true] [17592186217194 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349657 13194139535448 true] [17592186217195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349664 13194139535448 true] [17592186217195 1020 #edb/ref 17592186349671 13194139535448 true] [17592186217723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535448 true] [17592186217723 1100 "Given that $y_{0}(x) = e^{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$y^{′} = y^{2} - 2e^{x}y + e^{2x} + e^{x}$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139535448 false] [17592186217723 1100 "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x}y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\n \n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139535448 true] [17592186217723 1145 "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x}y+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x},\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=1,\\,b(x)=-2{e}^{x},\\,c(x)={e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{e}^{x}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+{e}^{x}=(z+{e}^{x})^{2}-2{e}^{x}(z+{e}^{x})+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & =({e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z+{z}^{2})-(2{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{x}z)+{e}^{2x}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′}+{e}^{x} & ={z}^{2}+{e}^{x} \\\\ {z}^{′} & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-{e}^{x}$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y-{e}^{x} & =-\\frac{1}{x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{x+C}+{e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{1}{x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535448 true] [17592186217737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535448 true] [17592186217737 1100 "The function $y_{0}(x) =-x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n$y^{′} =-y^{2} - (2x + 1)y - (1 + x + x^{2})$.\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n$\\frac{dz}{dx} + P(x)z = Q(x)z^{n}$\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$, and the value of $n$.$P(x) =$\n{{field-1}}\n$, Q(x) =$\n{{field-2}}\n$, n =$\n{{field-3}}\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"solving-riccati-differential-equations\"></a>" 13194139535448 false] [17592186217737 1100 "The function ${y}_{0}(x)=-x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-{y}^{2}-(2x+1)y-(1+x+{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186217737 1145 "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=-x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-1$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z-x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-1.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-1=-(z-x)^{2}-(2x+1)(-x+z)-(1+x+{x}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-1 & =-({x}^{2}+{z}^{2}-2xz)-(-2{x}^{2}+2xz-x+z)-(1+x+{x}^{2}) \\\\ {z}^{′}-1 & =-{z}^{2}-z-1 \\\\ {z}^{′}+z & =-{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=1,\\,Q(x)=-1,\\,n=2.\n$$" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349653 1034 "1" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349653 1111 #uuid "9eb032ba-854c-572f-b02d-5d5a59039885" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349654 1034 "-1" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349654 1111 #uuid "e78a88e7-3623-5181-90ba-2aee6d1dacae" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349655 1034 "-1" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349655 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349655 1111 #uuid "44f97dae-b00a-5efa-b871-3686cb439684" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349656 1034 "2" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349656 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349656 1111 #uuid "ea5ccfe0-b07b-566b-9318-1899942b3a79" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349658 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349660 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349662 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1089 "q-333616" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1100 "The function ${y}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)y+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2).\n$$\n\nExpress this equation in the Bernoulli form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nand state the functions $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ and the value of $n.$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,Q(x)=$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,n=$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1113 #uuid "3dbcebde-af6e-556b-a609-8e3b250e9430" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349657 1145 "A Riccati differential equation has the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x).\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)={x}^{2}.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=2x$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+{x}^{2}\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+2x.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+2x=x(z+{x}^{2})^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)(z+{x}^{2})+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2).\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+2x & =x(z+{x}^{2})^{2}-2x({x}^{2}+1)(z+{x}^{2})+x({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+2) \\\\ {z}^{′}+2x & =x{z}^{2}-2xz+2x \\\\ {z}^{′}+2xz & =x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a Bernoulli equation of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x){z}^{n}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x)=2x,\\,Q(x)=x,\\,n=2.\n$$" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349658 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349659 13194139535448 true] [17592186349658 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535448 true] [17592186349658 1041 "field-1" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349658 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349659 13194139535448 true] [17592186349658 1110 #uuid "fc12e19a-1bed-54e0-9879-4e3b17d20c5a" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349659 1034 "2x" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349659 1111 #uuid "20316b5e-87ee-58b6-9453-df38791ade65" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349660 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349661 13194139535448 true] [17592186349660 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535448 true] [17592186349660 1041 "field-2" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349660 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349661 13194139535448 true] [17592186349660 1110 #uuid "3c5c1ea3-35b6-518c-8e50-d3236963f495" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349661 1034 "x" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349661 1111 #uuid "94de50b2-d6b0-5dd7-8825-1aa2c9bc4b07" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349663 13194139535448 true] [17592186349662 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535448 true] [17592186349662 1041 "field-3" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349662 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349663 13194139535448 true] [17592186349662 1110 #uuid "96b328f5-a3b7-56ce-b6a0-9956feba25ec" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349663 1034 "2" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349663 1111 #uuid "c8e0cf2a-1d05-5ea6-8d76-f6519ae06de5" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349664 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349665 13194139535448 true] [17592186349664 1089 "q-334117" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349664 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535448 true] [17592186349664 1100 "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=3x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}y+18{x}^{3}+3\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139535448 true] [17592186349664 1113 #uuid "262f720c-cbdd-503c-9647-53ea02489b2a" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349664 1145 "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x\\,{y}^{2}-12{x}^{2}y+18{x}^{3}+3,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=2x,\\,b(x)=-12{x}^{2},\\,c(x)=18{x}^{3}+3.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=3x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=3$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z+3x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}+3.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}+3=2x\\,(z+3x)^{2}-12{x}^{2}(z+3x)+18{x}^{3}+3.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}+3 & =2x(9{x}^{2}+6xz+{z}^{2})-12{x}^{2}z-36{x}^{3}+18{x}^{3}+3 \\\\ {z}^{′}+3 & =2x{z}^{2}+3 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =2x{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y-3x$ to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y-3x & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}+3x \\\\  & =3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349666 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349667 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349668 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349669 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349670 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1041 "selection" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349667 13194139535448 true] [17592186349665 1110 #uuid "736d0edf-2620-5ef7-a342-b4bde0a23520" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349666 1034 "y=3x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+C}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349666 1111 #uuid "81538363-f3f8-5430-a0ee-e99fffd573b5" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349667 1034 "y=3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349667 1111 #uuid "479cf870-ce0d-5c84-837a-713e220be050" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349668 1034 "y=3x+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-C}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349668 1111 #uuid "0b0d8718-4b2f-5b6a-9b1e-eee0f30f5489" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349669 1034 "y=3x-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}+C}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349669 1111 #uuid "f0cc9a0f-889f-5fbe-ad4f-6ce5717bbd9d" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349670 1034 "y=3x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+C}" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535448 true] [17592186349670 1111 #uuid "144a4dcb-44b9-5d8c-ae73-8d1ba11faddb" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349671 1017 #edb/ref 17592186349672 13194139535448 true] [17592186349671 1089 "q-334144" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349671 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535448 true] [17592186349671 1100 "Given that ${y}_{0}(x)=-6x$ is a particular solution of the Riccati differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}+36xy+108{x}^{2}-6\n$$\n\nfind the general solution of the equation." 13194139535448 true] [17592186349671 1113 #uuid "4f6a3026-fcc0-5aa9-8872-9a4b820d514c" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349671 1145 "The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=3{y}^{2}+36xy+108{x}^{2}-6,\n$$\n\nis a Riccati differential equation of the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=a(x){y}^{2}+b(x)y+c(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\na(x)=3,\\,b(x)=36x,\\,c(x)=108{x}^{2}-6.\n$$\n\nTo reduce the given Riccati equation to a Bernoulli equation, we use the substitution\n\n$$\ny(x)=z(x)+{y}_{0}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere ${y}_{0}(x)$ is a known particular solution.\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)={z}^{′}(x)+{y}_{0}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nIn our case, ${y}_{0}(x)=-6x.$ Since ${y}_{0}^{′}(x)=-6$, we have\n\n$$\ny=z-6x\\,⇒\\,{y}^{′}={z}^{′}-6.\n$$\n\nLet's substitute these expressions into our Riccati equation:\n\n$$\n{z}^{′}-6=3(z-6x)^{2}+36x(z-6x)+108{x}^{2}-6.\n$$\n\nNow, we expand the right-hand side, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}-6 & =3(36{x}^{2}-12xz+{z}^{2})+36xz-216{x}^{2}+108{x}^{2}-6 \\\\ {z}^{′}-6 & =3{z}^{2}-6 \\\\ {z}^{′} & =3{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve the obtained equation using separation of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x} & =3 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {z}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int 3\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{z} & =3x+C \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nFinally, let's substitute $z=y+6x$ (that is, $y=z-6x$) to recover the initial variable $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y+6x & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{1}{3x+C}-6x \\\\  & =-6x-\\frac{1}{3x+C}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349673 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349674 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349675 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349676 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1000 #edb/ref 17592186349677 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1041 "selection" 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1104 #edb/ref 17592186349674 13194139535448 true] [17592186349672 1110 #uuid "24c82e7b-4e55-535b-a69e-435cf64004e3" 131941